Third-party components and how they are used
--------------------------------------------

Qt 6 (QtCore, QtGui, QtQml, QtQuick, QtQuick Controls 2, QtQuick Layouts,
QtNetwork, QtSvg)
    License: LGPL-3.0 (used modules); some modules are GPL-3.0-only and are
    NOT used by this project.
    Linking: dynamically linked shared libraries. Users may replace the Qt
    libraries with their own builds (relinking); the build system does not
    static-link Qt and does not strip the ability to substitute the libraries.
    No GPL-only Qt module (Qt Charts, Qt Virtual Keyboard, Qt Data
    Visualization, Qt Graphs) is used: the live graphs are drawn in QML Canvas.

libfuse3
    License: LGPL-2.1-or-later.
    Linking: dynamically linked (Linux). Notice reproduced here as required;
    the library is not modified.

Rust dependencies
    Every crate in the dependency graph passes the allowlist in deny.toml
    (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, MPL-2.0, Unicode, CC0, Unlicense,
    AGPL-3.0, GPL-3.0). The full mapping is in docs/licensing.md.

Jottacloud API
    The API is used as a client, over HTTPS, with the user's own credentials.
    This project contains no Jottacloud code and no Jottacloud trademark beyond
    the descriptive name.

Corresponding source
    Source for every released binary is this repository at the released tag,
    plus the release assets' source archive. AGPL-3.0 sections 4-6 are
    satisfied by shipping the complete corresponding source alongside each
    release.
